--- comparison operators do not chain: one E1010 at the second operator, parsing continues left associatively
a < b < c
---
a <= b > c
---
a > b >= c
---
a == b == c
---
a != b == c
--- a long chain is still one diagnostic
a < b < c < d < e
--- two separate chains are two diagnostics
a < b < c && d == e == f
--- a different level after the chain is fine
a < b < c == d
--- parentheses state the grouping, and different levels combine without error
(a < b) < c
---
a < b == c
